# EmailJS Configuration
# Get your credentials from https://www.emailjs.com/

# 1. Sign up for a free account at https://www.emailjs.com/
# 2. Create an email service (Gmail, Outlook, etc.)
# 3. Create an email template with the following variables:
#    - {{from_name}} - Sender's name
#    - {{from_email}} - Sender's email
#    - {{message}} - Message content
#    - {{to_email}} - Your email (jahnavisingh6@gmail.com)
# 4. Copy your Service ID, Template ID, and Public Key below

NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=service_xxxxxxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=template_xxxxxxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=YOUR_PUBLIC_KEY

# After adding your credentials:
# 1. Rename this file from .env.local.example to .env.local
# 2. Replace the values above with your actual EmailJS credentials
# 3. Restart your development server (npm run dev)
